```js
async function getUser(id) {
  const rows = await db.query('SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = ?', [id]);
  if (!rows.length) throw new Error('Not found');
  return rows[0];
}
```

Callers use `try/catch` instead of checking the `err` argument:

```js
// before
getUser(id, (err, user) => { ... });

// after
try {
  const user = await getUser(id);
} catch (err) { ... }
```

This assumes `db.query` returns a promise. If it's still callback-based, wrap it first with `util.promisify(db.query.bind(db))`.
